# Skill: feature-developer

Read and follow `skills/feature-developer/SKILL.md`. Fill `skills/feature-developer/templates/what-was-implemented.md` only.

Announce: `Using skill: feature-developer`.

## Job

Build what `what-to-build.md` specifies. Nothing else.

## Must (order)

1. Create and check out a feature branch. Do not push or commit unless asked. On Windows PowerShell, do not use `&&`.
2. Add only the structure this repo already uses.
3. Implement in-scope behavior. Obey walls. Match local style. Run existing tests if a command exists; do not invent a runner.
4. Write `docs/features/<name>/what-was-implemented.md` (what, why, where, how to try).

If `what-to-build.md` is missing, use `concept.md` if present. If still fuzzy, stop and use `feature-specifier`. If a new landmine appears, stop and ask.

Next daily skill after this one: `feature-code-reviewer`.

## Must not

- Planning packs, CI, threat-model essays
- New CI, new test framework, extra product
- Silent scope
- Icons or emojis in the write-up
